---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | PowerBI.tips"
  description="Privacy policy and privacy rights information for PowerBI.tips."
>
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg text-neutral-600">
      This page restores privacy-policy content that appears to have existed on the previous site under the About section,
      including general privacy rights and California privacy rights references.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose max-w-none">
    <p>
      PowerBI.tips respects your privacy. We collect only the information needed to operate the site, improve the user
      experience, deliver requested services, and communicate about our content, tools, events, and training offerings.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we may collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Contact information you provide directly, such as name and email address</li>
      <li>Usage information such as pages visited, referring links, browser type, and device information</li>
      <li>Information submitted through forms, newsletter signups, event registrations, or training inquiries</li>
      <li>Basic cookie and analytics data needed to understand site performance and improve the experience</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Operate, maintain, and improve the PowerBI.tips website and related services</li>
      <li>Respond to questions, requests, registrations, and support inquiries</li>
      <li>Send updates you requested, including newsletters, events, training, or product information</li>
      <li>Protect the site, prevent abuse, and understand how content and tools are being used</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing of information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal information. We may share limited information with service providers that help us run the
      site, analytics, email communication, events, or training operations. Those providers are expected to process data
      only as needed to deliver their services.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      PowerBI.tips may use cookies or similar technologies to improve site functionality, remember preferences, measure
      traffic, and understand how visitors engage with the site. You can usually control cookies through your browser
      settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your location, you may have rights related to access, correction, deletion, or limitation of the use
      of your personal information. California residents may also have additional privacy rights under applicable law.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you would like to make a privacy-related request, contact us and include enough information for us to understand
      and respond to your request.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      This site may link to third-party websites, tools, and services. We are not responsible for the privacy practices
      of those external sites. Please review their policies directly.
    </p>

    <h2>Policy updates</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time as the site, tools, services, or legal requirements change. Updates
      will be reflected on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, please contact PowerBI.tips through the appropriate contact or training channels listed on
      the site.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500">
      Note: the original migrated WordPress source for this policy was not recoverable in the local migration artifacts,
      so this page is a reconstructed policy page based on the prior site structure and intended legal/privacy content.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

</BaseLayout>
